# Dora the Explorer — project rules

Dora the Explorer is a native macOS 26 file explorer (Windows 11 File Explorer parity where the platform allows).
AppKit lifecycle app (`NSApplicationDelegate`, `@main` on `AppDelegate`, no SwiftUI `App` struct), Swift 6 language mode, strict concurrency. Bundle ID `com.dorasoft.dora`. Hardened Runtime on, App Sandbox OFF.

## 1. Hard architecture rules

1. **No disk I/O, metadata fetch, directory enumeration, sort of >5k items, or thumbnail decode on the main thread.** All of it in `actor` or `nonisolated` code handing back `Sendable` values. FSCore calls `assertNotMainThreadForIO()` at the top of every enumeration/stat/metadata entry point.
2. **No SwiftUI `List`, `LazyVGrid`, `LazyVStack`, `ForEach` for directory contents.** Directory contents render in AppKit collection views: `NSTableView` (Details) and `NSCollectionView` (Icons/List/Tiles/Content) with reuse and prefetching, wrapped by `NSViewRepresentable` only where needed.
3. **One selection model, one controller.** Every content view implements `FileListController`; selection, keyboard, drag/drop, rename and grouping live there, not per view.
4. **Layered:** App (windows/tabs/chrome) → AppCore (state, commands) → feature packages. Packages never import the app target. Feature packages never import each other except through `FSCore` models and `DesignSystem`.
5. **Lazy metadata.** `FileItem` is a small `Sendable` struct (ids, url, name, flags, size, dates). Anything expensive (EXIF, ID3, dimensions, git status) is fetched by a separate async service keyed by item and cached.
6. **No third-party dependency without a note in `docs/ARCHITECTURE.md`**, and none for things in the standard library/frameworks. Planned exceptions only: Sparkle (Phase 19) and libarchive (Phase 15), both justified.

## 2. Swift 6 concurrency

- `swiftLanguageMode(.v6)`, strict concurrency in every package and the app target.
- All cross-actor types `Sendable`. No `@unchecked Sendable` without a comment explaining the invariant.
- All `Task`s that outlive their scope are stored and cancelled; no orphan `Task.detached` without a stored handle.
- Actors for shared mutable state; `@MainActor` + `@Observable` for UI models. Never block the main thread on an actor.
- Subsystem loggers: `Logger(subsystem: "com.dorasoft.dora", category: <feature>)`.

## 3. Performance budgets (verifiable, not vibes)

| Operation | Budget |
|---|---|
| First batch of a 100k-file folder | < 100 ms (Apple Silicon, local APFS) |
| Details view scroll, 100k items | 120 fps, 0 animation hitches in 10 s |
| Sort switch, 100k items | < 150 ms |
| Tab switch | < 16 ms |
| View switch | < 50 ms |
| Home first paint (cached) | < 200 ms |
| Search first result, indexed home | < 150 ms |
| Command bar / context menu open | < 50 ms |

Every budget gets an `OSSignposter` interval and an XCTest performance test. CI fails on >15% regression only for deterministic tests; timing-sensitive tests are local-only.

## 4. Correctness rules

- **Unicode**: compare and group on NFC.
- **Paths**: use `URL`, never string concatenation. Handle `:` and `/` in names and long paths.
- **Errors surface**: every failure is handled, retried, or shown. No `try?` that swallows a recoverable error. Log with the error attached.
- **Destructive ops** (trash, delete, overwrite, extract) go through `FileOps` and are undoable or confirmed.
- **Zip-slip / traversal / symlink escape / decompression bombs** are rejected, each with a test fixture.

## 5. API discipline

- Only use Apple APIs that exist in the installed SDK. If a symbol is uncertain, verify in the SDK before writing code. Never invent APIs.
- Glass on macOS 26: SwiftUI `.glassEffect(_:in:)` / `GlassEffectContainer` / `.glassEffectID` hosted in an `NSHostingView`, or `NSVisualEffectView` materials with solid fallbacks. `NSGlassEffectView` does not exist.
- Respect Reduce Transparency, Increase Contrast and Reduce Motion. Text-bearing surfaces use opaque backgrounds.

## 6. Accessibility & localization

- Every interactive control has an accessibility label and value; rows announce name, kind, size, date.
- No hard-coded user-facing strings: use the String Catalog. Layout must survive 30% string expansion and RTL.

## 7. Tests

- Each package ships unit tests; each phase adds tests for its acceptance criteria plus perf tests where a budget exists.
- Deterministic temp-directory fixtures. No network in unit tests.
- `make test` must pass before any phase is reported done.

## 8. Commits

- One commit per phase, message prefixed `[Cursor] `, tests green at commit.
- Never commit `build/`, `DerivedData/`, or `.DS_Store`.
